<article class="env-theorem" id="03QL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03QL">Theorem <span data-tag="03QL">59.32.8</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a local ring and $\kappa \subset \kappa ^{sep}$ a separable algebraic closure. There exist canonical flat local ring maps $R \to R^ h \to R^{sh}$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R^ h$, $R^{sh}$ are filtered colimits of étale $R$-algebras, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R^ h$ is henselian, $R^{sh}$ is strictly henselian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathfrak m R^ h$ (resp. $\mathfrak m R^{sh}$) is the maximal ideal of $R^ h$ (resp. $R^{sh}$), and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\kappa = R^ h/\mathfrak m R^ h$, and $\kappa ^{sep} = R^{sh}/\mathfrak m R^{sh}$ as extensions of $\kappa $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The structure of $R^ h$ and $R^{sh}$ is described in Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/04GN" data-tag="04GN">10.155.1</a> and <a href="/tag/04GP" data-tag="04GP">10.155.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>